{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q6589967","formula":"C₂₃H₃₂N₂O₂","hill":"C23H32N2O2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":23.0,"H":32.0,"N":2.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"SA-4503"},"descriptions":{"en":"Cutamesine (SA 4503) is a synthetic sigma receptor agonist which is selective for the σ1 receptor, a chaperone protein mainly found in the endoplasmic reticulum of cells in the central nervous system. These σ1 receptors play a key role in the modulation of Ca2+ release and apoptosis. Cutamesine's activation of the σ1 receptor is tied to a variety of physiological phenomena in the CNS, including activation of dopamine-releasing neurons and repression of the MAPK/ERK pathway."},"fame":8,"pubchemCid":9907323,"mass":368.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"COC1=C(C=C(C=C1)CCN2CCN(CC2)CCCC3=CC=CC=C3)OC","inchikey":"UVSWWUWQVAQPJR-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"1-[2-(3,4-dimethoxyphenyl)ethyl]-4-(3-phenylpropyl)piperazine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"9907323","atoms":59,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":6.776,"y":-1.947,"z":-0.952,"el":"O"},{"x":8.117,"y":0.479,"z":-1.134,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.243,"y":-0.318,"z":0.877,"el":"N"},{"x":0.553,"y":0.417,"z":0.808,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.252,"y":-1.008,"z":1.711,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.825,"y":1.067,"z":0.626,"el":"C"},{"x":0.134,"y":-0.967,"z":1.059,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.438,"y":1.11,"z":-0.025,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.564,"y":-0.356,"z":1.5,"el":"C"},{"x":1.873,"y":0.455,"z":0.183,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.655,"y":-0.206,"z":0.44,"el":"C"},{"x":2.976,"y":0.245,"z":1.221,"el":"C"},{"x":-6.048,"y":-0.266,"z":1.071,"el":"C"},{"x":4.346,"y":0.304,"z":0.593,"el":"C"},{"x":-7.135,"y":-0.082,"z":0.043,"el":"C"},{"x":4.939,"y":-0.859,"z":0.104,"el":"C"},{"x":5.02,"y":1.522,"z":0.502,"el":"C"},{"x":-7.606,"y":1.197,"z":-0.252,"el":"C"},{"x":-7.669,"y":-1.191,"z":-0.61